{
  "_comment": [
    "Approximate camera locations, derived from the place names the cameras",
    "themselves carry \u2014 the organiser's grid labels and the text burned into",
    "each frame. This file exists because the authoritative catalogue",
    "(cameras.json) requires a signed-in session we do not hold, and without",
    "coordinates the map cannot be populated at all.",
    "",
    "EVERY ENTRY IS APPROXIMATE AND SAYS SO. `precision` is the honest bound:",
    "  LANDMARK  ~150 m   a specific named junction, bridge or building",
    "  LOCALITY  ~1.5 km  a named neighbourhood or village",
    "  CITY      ~6 km    only the town is known",
    "These are NOT surveyed camera positions. They place a camera near the",
    "right junction so an investigator can reason about corridors; they must",
    "never be used as evidence of where a vehicle was, and the interface",
    "labels every one of them as derived rather than authoritative.",
    "",
    "When the catalogue becomes reachable, its coordinates supersede all of",
    "this \u2014 `make government-import` overwrites them and the provenance",
    "changes from DERIVED_FROM_NAME to CATALOGUE."
  ],
